                <pb facs="0657" n="553" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg553"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4696a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Switzerland
                        (Wilson), at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-10T19:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1932—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. At the press conference this morning the question was asked, presumably on
                    the basis of newspaper reports, whether the United States was planning to take
                    the 31st infantry out of Shanghai and the answer was made that we have no
                    present intention of withdrawing the 31st infantry and that the question of
                    withdrawal is not under consideration.</p>
                <p>You may so inform inquirers.</p>
                <p>For your confidential information and guidance, in case such reports are brought
                    to your attention and questions are asked by responsible persons: some
                    discussion of such a possible move appears to have been indulged in by some
                    American authorities in the Far East.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
